### *Part 3: Concept to Code Translation - My Reference Guide*

*I asked: Show path operation decorators*
# Path operation decorators = @app.get/post/put/delete etc
# They are same function, different HTTP method

@app.get("/items") # READ list - idempotent, cacheable
def list_items():...

@app.post("/items", status_code=201) # CREATE - not idempotent
def create_item(item: Item):...

@app.put("/items/{id}") # REPLACE whole object
def update_item(id: int, item: Item):...

@app.patch("/items/{id}") # UPDATE partial - common mistake: use PUT when you mean PATCH
def patch_item(id: int, item: ItemPatch):...

@app.delete("/items/{id}", status_code=204) # DELETE - 204 no content standard
def delete_item(id: int):...
*Background Tasks from docs:*
from fastapi import BackgroundTasks

def write_log(email: str):
    with open("log.txt","a") as f: f.write(f"sent to {email}\n")

@app.post("/send-email/")
def send_email(email: str, background_tasks: BackgroundTasks):
    # Response returns immediately, email sent after
    background_tasks.add_task(write_log, email)
    return {"message":"Email will be sent"}
# Use when: email, analytics, cache invalidation - not for critical DB writes
